  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Design Theme**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design HTML to extract the \"Frosted Glass\" theme elements. Specifically, I\'m focusing on identifying and replicating styling and layout patterns, starting with the provided theme colors like `bg-slate-950` and `text-slate-100`. I plan to integrate these into the existing app components.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the visual elements: mesh gradients are the initial focus, implemented via CSS classes and added to the `App.tsx` file for a base layout. Next, I\'ll incorporate the defined containers with their blurred backgrounds and borders (`bg-white/5 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/10` etc.) I\'ll also bring in the text accent colors. I\'m building out the basic app structure as planned, starting with `Navbar.tsx`, `Hero.tsx`, and so on.\n\n\n**Refining Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `Navbar` component, adding the header with `flex` properties and the \"Frosted Glass\" styling: rounded corners, shadows, and blur effects. I\'ve also incorporated the `Shield` icon and adjusted text color to match the design theme. I am currently updating the styling of the title in the header with the `VerifiedSlots` details.\n\n\n**Adjusting Styles, Adding Content**\n\nI am now focused on incorporating new content and styles into the existing `Navbar` structure. I am paying close attention to integrating these elements without altering the overall layout. The goal is a seamless application of the \"Frosted Glass\" theme to the existing components. Currently, I\'m integrating the provided header content, ensuring it fits perfectly within the existing flex structure. My main priority is a visually appealing and cohesive integration of the \"Frosted Glass\" theme.\n\n\n**Adapting Layout to Theme**\n\nI\'m now determining how to integrate the 3-column grid design into the existing application structure, since I must keep `Hero`, `ProsCons`, `TrustAndSafety`, and `Comparison` as separate components. I\'m choosing to apply the styling and layout patterns directly to these components as vertical sections because restructuring the main content layout isn\'t allowed. I\'m now looking into `Hero.tsx` to begin the integration process.\n\n\n**Integrating New Component Design**\n\nI\'m now changing the `Hero.tsx` section\'s styling and structure to fit the \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I\'ve switched from the old `bg-slate-50` with a border to a `bg-white/5 backdrop-blur-md` design. I\'ve added a frosted, rounded container around the content. I\'m focusing on the `Verified Review` label and adjusting it to match the provided specifications. I\'m aiming for a seamless visual flow.\n\n\n**Refining Verified Review Design**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Verified Review\" badge. I\'m focusing on the animation and styling. The existing code provided the basis, but I have adjusted the `animate` properties to achieve the required visual effect. I\'ve integrated it into the `Hero` section. I\'m also now updating the review headline and introductory text.\n\n\n**Considering Layout Structure**\n\nI\'m now contemplating how the 3-column grid design applies to `App.tsx` and the structure of my separate components. I\'m choosing to apply a grid to the existing application structure, since keeping the components as separate sections is crucial. I\'ll test how applying the grid to the `App.tsx` structure affects layout, especially concerning the `Hero` section. I\'ll evaluate the layout impact of grid application on separate content sections.\n\n\n**Revising Component Layout**\n\nI\'m now determining how to integrate the 3-column design while accommodating the internal layout of components like `ProsCons`. Since `ProsCons` already contains two columns, directly fitting it into the 3-column layout would cause squishing. I plan to adjust `ProsCons` to match the smaller stacked Pros/Cons block, ensuring it fits into the grid structure. I am now modifying the component\'s internal design to work within the 3-column layout.\n\n\n**Adapting ProsCons Component**\n\nI\'m now changing the `ProsCons` component. The original two-column layout is proving problematic within the new grid. I plan to convert the Pros and Cons into a stacked list design, with separate visual sections for each. I\'m focusing on ensuring it fits the new 3-column layout without unwanted content compression, while preserving the existing pros and cons layout.\n\n\n**Refining Section Styling**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `TrustAndSafety` component, focusing on the correct visual representation of the \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I\'ve applied the provided `bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-lg` styling to achieve the intended blurred background. Now I am using the `rounded-3xl` corners, matching the established design. The component will fit nicely into the new 3-column layout. I am also planning the integration of `Zap` and `Shield` icons.\n\n\n**Integrating New Safety Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided safety audit and license details into the `TrustAndSafety` component. I\'m focusing on incorporating the visual elements, such as the `Security Audit Passed` badge with the animation, into the frosted glass design to enhance the overall theme. I am now incorporating the Curacao License section and ensuring the layout remains consistent with the established design principles.\n\n\n**Implementing Safety Features**\n\nI am now implementing the payout efficiency section. I\'m focusing on integrating the provided payout data and visual elements. I\'ll include the 24-hour crypto payout and the progress bar styling, matching the design theme. I will also incorporate the expert note, and ensure it seamlessly blends with the other components within the new layout. I\'m aiming for a visually cohesive display.\n\n\n**Integrating Comparison Component**\n\nI am now focusing on implementing the `Comparison` component. I\'m applying the \"Frosted Glass\" theme