ndSafety\";\nimport { Comparison } from \"./components/Comparison\";\nimport { Disclaimer } from \"./components/Disclaimer\";\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"min-h-screen bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 font-sans relative overflow-x-hidden flex flex-col selection:bg-blue-500/30 selection:text-blue-200\">\n      {/* Background Mesh Gradients */}\n      <div className=\"absolute inset-0 z-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-700 to-slate-800 opacity-50 dark:opacity-80 blur-2xl\"></div>\n\n      <Navbar />\n\n      <main className=\"container mx-auto px-4 py-8 z-10\">\n        <Hero />\n        <ProsCons />\n        <TrustAndSafety />\n        <Comparison />\n        <Disclaimer />\n      </main>\n\n      <footer className=\"bg-white/5 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/10 rounded-3xl py-6 mt-8 z-10 mx-4\">\n        <div className=\"flex items-center justify-center space-x-4 mb-4\">\n          <div className=\"w-8 h-8 border border-white/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-[10px] font-bold text-white text-center leading-tight\">RNG<br/>CERT</div>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\"text-center pb-6\">\n          <p className=\"text-[10px] text-slate-600\">\n            &copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} VerifiedSlots. All rights reserved.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </footer>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n\n**Revising the App Structure**\n\nI am now structuring the app using a grid layout to accommodate a 3-column design, affecting the component arrangement in `App.tsx`. The main content is now within a grid with `Hero`, `ProsCons`, `TrustAndSafety`, and `Comparison` components organized into a `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3` layout. I\'ve also incorporated the disclaimer at the end.\n\n\n**Refining Navbar Component**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the `Navbar` component. I\'m incorporating the shield icon, the header text and the stars into the component. I am optimizing the layout for responsiveness across various screen sizes. I am adjusting spacing to ensure optimal visual balance.\n\n\n**Optimizing Navbar Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the `Navbar` component, restoring the navigation links `Reviews`, `Bonuses`, and `Guides`, per the design. I am now incorporating the shield icon into the header. I\'m adjusting the layout to accommodate these elements and optimize responsiveness across devices.\n\n\n**Restructuring the App Content**\n\nI am now implementing the responsive 3-column grid design for the content sections. I\'m focusing on the responsive behavior of the columns, especially on mobile devices. I\'ve integrated `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3` to implement the responsive layout. I am evaluating how the different screen sizes affect the presentation of each section.\n\n\n\n**Optimizing Navbar Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the `Navbar` component, restoring the navigation links `Reviews`, `Bonuses`, and `Guides`, per the design. I am now incorporating the shield icon into the header. I\'m adjusting the layout to accommodate these elements and optimize responsiveness across devices.\n\n\n**Refining Content Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided headline, intro text, and welcome bonus details into the existing `Hero` section. I\'ve structured the section content with `flex` properties and padding. I\'m focusing on ensuring it matches the visual specifications.\n\n\n**Adjusting Section Placement**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the placement and order of the sections within the grid layout. I am ensuring that the visual flow is intuitive and that the responsive design is functioning as expected, particularly on mobile devices. I am carefully evaluating the arrangement of `Hero`, `ProsCons`, `TrustAndSafety`, and `Comparison` to optimize user experience.\n\nI\'m now integrating the `Hero` content, as provided, into the existing layout. I\'ve ensured a cohesive integration by paying close attention to visual consistency. I\'m focusing on text and color consistency to match the overall theme.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the visual consistency across the app, especially integrating the header text and welcome bonus. I am making adjustments to fonts, colors, and layout, and ensuring the `Verified Review` label is placed correctly. I am now incorporating the review headline and introductory text.\n\n\n**Integrating New Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided welcome bonus and game library details into the existing `Hero` section. I\'ve placed these new visual elements, applying design classes and styles to ensure a clean visual integration within the established \"Frosted Glass\" theme and new grid layout, with text-color adjustments and matching icons.\n\nI am now structuring the `Hero` section with the addition of the new content. I am now evaluating the visual consistency across the app.\n\n\n**Adapting Component for Grid**\n\nI\'m now changing the `ProsCons` component\'s structure. The previous 2-column layout within a grid item caused issues, so I am adjusting it to be a single-column layout. I am integrating individual elements into list items, adjusting padding and margins. I\'ll maintain a consistent design within the new 3-column grid structure.\n\n\n**Finalizing ProsCons Adaptation**\n\nI\'m now changing the `ProsCons` component further, improving the list design. I am converting pros/cons content to a structured list, and adding visual consistency with the other components. I am adjusting the spacing and visual elements to fit the 3-column layout seamlessly.\n\nI\'m now ensuring the updated content displays as expected within the three-column layout. I am evaluating text size, padding, and margins, and how this fits within the grid design.\n\n\n**Refining Safety Component**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `TrustAndSafety` component with the grid layout, ensuring the correct styling, including the rounded corners and blurred background, which fits the \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I\'m focusing on ensuring its content, including safety features and license details, integrates correctly within the new three-column layout. I\'m adding `Zap` and `Shield` icons.\n\n\n**Adjusting Content Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the `TrustAndSafety` section, ensuring the styling and the incorporation of the security badge. I\'ve integrated safety audit details into the `TrustAndSafety` component, integrating the rounded corners and blurred background to fit the \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I am including the `Zap` and `Shield` icons, and checking the placement of all the elements.\n\n\n**Integrating Safety Features**\n\nI am now integrating the provided Curacao License and payment speed details into the existing `TrustAndSafety` component, ensuring the visual styling matches the theme. The license and payment speed descriptions are integrated with the existing `Zap` and `Shield` icons for visual coherence.\n\n\n**Adapting Comparison Component**\n\nI\'m now adapting the `Comparison` component to fit the 3-column grid, maintaining the table structure. I\'ll retain the table but integrate it into the \"Frosted Glass\" theme by applying appropriate styling. I\'ll focus on ensuring it maintains readability and visual appeal within the grid layout, while keeping the data intact. I am adapting the styling to improve its appearance and visual integration.\n\n\n**Refining Comparison Component**\n\nI\'ve decided to restructure the application layout. My plan involves positioning `ProsCons` and `TrustAndSafety` in a two-column grid, followed by `Comparison` spanning the full width. This keeps the table in the correct format. I am also planning on modifying the `Comparison` component to make sure it will overflow (`overflow-x-auto`).\n\nI\'m now revising the `App.tsx` layout to reflect the new grid approach. The `Comparison` component now follows the two columns, and the table content\'s width is fully preserved. I am now updating the table\'s visual styling to enhance its integration with the \"Frosted Glass\" theme.\n\n\n**Optimizing Table Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the `Comparison` table. I am adding a new table header with a comparison title. I\'ve integrated `overflow-x-auto` to handle wider content. I am now updating the table\'s visual styling to enhance its integration with the \"Frosted Glass\" theme.\n\nI\'m now revising the table\'s visual styling to enhance its integration with the \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I\'ve added a new table header with a comparison title.\n\n\n**Refining Table Design**\n\nI am now focusing on integrating the provided comparison table data and styling. I am using the provided data and I\'m updating table\'s visual styling to match the grid layout and \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I\'m focusing on ensuring its readability and visual appeal within the layout.\n\n\n**Finalizing Visual Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided disclaimer into the layout, applying the theme. I\'ve placed the disclaimer within a themed footer, styled to match the \"Frosted Glass\" design. The styling aims to enhance readability and ensure consistent integration across the application.\n\n\n**Finalizing Component Styling**\n\nI\'m now integrating the SSL/RNG badges and disclaimer text into the footer, styled to match the theme. I\'ve ensured all legal details are present, styled consistently. The focus is on a clear and cohesive presentation of the final legal elements.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Integration and Design**\n\nI\'m now completing the integration, incorporating the provided helpline information into the footer alongside existing legal details. I\'ve ensured seamless visual integration. I\'m focusing on ensuring its readability and a consistent \"Frosted Glass\" aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining Final App Design**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the app\'s visual integration and layout. I am integrating the provided helpline information into the footer alongside existing legal details. I\'ve ensured a cohesive visual integration for all components, with a focus on readability and consistency with the \"Frosted Glass\" theme. I\'m also now reviewing the grid alignment.\n\n\n\n"
