  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Bonus Comparisons**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a bonus comparison table. I\'m structuring it to highlight key differences: percentages, maximums, wagering requirements, minimum deposits, validity periods, and any restrictions. This detailed analysis of bonus terms will give users a quick, useful summary.\n\n\n**Expanding Component Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the component scope, specifically integrating new components into `App.tsx` following the frosted glass design. I\'m focusing on creating and structuring the new components: `BonusComparison`, `BonusTerms`, `GameVariety`, and `PaymentMethods`, keeping the frosted glass aesthetic consistent. I\'m prioritizing the design and incorporation of these new components.\n\n\n**Refining Data Display**\n\nI\'m currently refining the data display within the `BonusComparison` component, ensuring the structure is easy to parse. I\'m focusing on incorporating real data and improving the table\'s readability. I\'ve switched to a comparison format, contrasting Apex Casino\'s metrics with those of a \"typical competitor.\"\n\n\n**Comparing Bonus Metrics**\n\nI\'m now comparing specific bonus metrics, such as percentage, maximums, wagering requirements, minimum deposits, and validity periods, using concrete data. I\'m focusing on contrasting Apex Casino\'s bonus terms against a competitor\'s, highlighting differences. I\'m structuring this data clearly within the `BonusComparison` component, using a table format with clear headings and visual distinctions.\n\n\n**Detailing Game Restrictions**\n\nI\'m now detailing game restrictions, specifically within the `BonusComparison` component. I\'m focusing on clearly showing that live casino games are excluded from bonus wagering, as opposed to competitor\'s, which include slots only. I\'m aiming for a concise table format to highlight these restrictions.\n\n\n**Clarifying Bonus Terms**\n\nI\'m now detailing specific bonus terms within the comparison table. I\'m focusing on highlighting the key aspects of the welcome bonus: a 100% match up to $500, with a 40x playthrough (80x bonus) on both deposit and bonus. The maximum bet during bonus play is capped at $5 per spin/round, exceeding which will result in the loss of funds and winnings.\n\n\n**Highlighting Game Contributions**\n\nI\'m now detailing game contributions to wagering requirements. I\'m structuring a section in the `BonusComparison` component to show that slots contribute 100%, table games 5%, and live dealer games 0%. My goal is clear and concise information.\n\n\n**Categorizing Game Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing major gaming categories. I\'m focusing on providing depth, structuring information into categories like video slots and table games. I\'m aiming for clarity in describing these categories.\n\n\n**Describing Game Options**\n\nI\'m now describing specific game options and categories. I\'m structuring a breakdown of both RNG-based traditional casino games, like European Roulette Pro, and the Live Dealer options, emphasizing those powered by Evolution Gaming and Pragmatic Play Live, using specific examples like Lightning Roulette and VIP Blackjack. My goal is clarity and conciseness.\n\n\n**Presenting Payment Details**\n\nI\'m now presenting the payment details within a new `PaymentMethods` component, offering a clear breakdown of deposit and withdrawal options. I\'m showcasing a transparent overview of banking options, highlighting zero hidden fees for standard transactions, and emphasizing any applicable network fees. I\'m structuring this information in a table format for clarity.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Payment Details**\n\nI\'m now structuring the payment details in a table within a dedicated component. I\'m focusing on clarifying deposit and withdrawal methods, along with processing times and potential fees for each. I\'ve designed the table with clear headings for method, type (currency), processing times for deposits and withdrawals, and any associated fees, for easy reference.\n\n\n**Clarifying Payment Times**\n\nI\'m now clarifying processing times within the `PaymentMethods` component table. I\'m focusing on highlighting the distinct processing times for various methods. I\'m using the table structure to show the fast instant deposit times for crypto and credit/debit options, against the slightly longer withdrawal times. This offers the user a very clear overview.\n\n\n**Organizing Component Layout**\n\nI\'m now organizing the component layout within `App.tsx`. I\'m focusing on the integration of new components, and their order: Hero, ProsCons/TrustAndSafety (two-column grid), BonusComparison, BonusTerms/GameVariety (two-column grid), and PaymentMethods. I\'m structuring a clear and logical flow, and assessing optimal grid layouts.\n\n\n**Adjusting Component Spacing**\n\nI\'m now revising the layout to accommodate component needs, particularly table-based components. I\'ve switched the layout of  `GameVariety` and `PaymentMethods` from a grid design to full-width components, and `BonusComparison` is also full-width to accommodate its table. This ensures readability and a clear, logical flow, especially for tabular content.\n\n\n"
