  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Markdown Support**\n\nI\'ve realized I need to clarify the user\'s need regarding Markdown. It seems they might want a `.md` file, or possibly a React component to display markdown content. I\'m focusing on the best way to handle the user\'s request.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Markdown Output**\n\nI\'ve decided creating the `bitz-review.md` file is still a good idea, as it keeps options open. However, I\'ve re-focused on directly providing Markdown output within my response, since that\'s what the user asked for. I will also generate the file to keep the code consistent. The review generation will be my next step.\n\n\n**Analyzing Casino Regulations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of Bitz Casino, assessing its regulatory standing, especially regarding the Dutch market. My focus is the legal framework. I\'m prioritizing the compliance aspects. It\'s clear that it lacks a KSA license. This is critical in the analysis, affecting safety. I need to emphasize the lack of player protection in the Netherlands.\n\n\n**Assessing Casino Risks**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the risks of Bitz Casino. I\'ve uncovered that it\'s an offshore operation lacking Dutch KSA and European licensing, which means it cannot legally accept players from the Netherlands. This lack of compliance exposes players to potential harm, as they waive legal protection, and have few payout guarantees. Cryptocurrency further complicates accountability. The bonus terms appear predatory as the wagering requirements are high.\n\n\n**Evaluating Bonus Terms**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the bonus structure of Bitz.io, specifically the wagering requirements and game contribution limits. The bonus terms seem very restrictive, making it extremely difficult to convert bonus funds into withdrawable cash. The strict contribution limits and betting caps further reduce the value, making it less attractive than presented. I need to make sure to detail these terms to the user.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI\'m also reviewing the payment methods. Bitz.io is a crypto-first casino, so it only supports Bitcoin, Ethereum, and some altcoins. I\'ve noted that deposits are quick, but withdrawals can take up to a day. Crucially, I\'m noting that Dutch players cannot use iDEAL or SEPA transfers which are standard for safe, regulated casinos. I\'m considering if I should update the React app in line with my past actions, and if so, how.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 36
      nanos: 9443276
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
